  "intro_html": "<p>Badus is said to mean steep, reclining. But the same mountain has a second name, Six Madun. Six is a rock head, Madun (Madone) is a pillar or a column. Correspondingly the access via Six Madun Egg is a steep, inclined ramp with a rocky head.</p>\n<p>From Lai da Tuma a side trip of about 20 minutes brings you to the beautifully located Badushütte.</p>",
